  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "上古時期中國文明的起源與發展",
    "sub_ename": "ANCIENT CHINA AND THE FORMATION OF CHINA AS A STATE",
    "describe_ch": "本課程根據中國考古學的重要考古發現與研究成果，介紹文明的起源與上古時期的社會發展脈絡，時間起迄為新石器時代至漢代初年，主題涵蓋全新世初期動植物的馴化（黍、粟、稻、犬、豬、雞），外來動植物的影響、農業在新石器中期的蓬勃發展，人口擴張在仰韶、龍山時代所帶來的社會變革、各種工藝技術的發展歷程、文字的發明、青銅時代王朝的興衰解構、東周時期的區域化發展、兵器與戰爭型態自商代至東周時期的轉變、秦漢帝國的大一統、物質文化所反映的秦漢世俗社會，以及華夏以外的異域。",
    "describe_eh": "This course introduces the origins and the context of social development in ancient China, from the Neolithic to the early Han Dynasty, based on the important archaeological discoveries and research in Chinese Archaeology. Course topics include the domestication of animals and plants in the Holocene (i.e. millet, rice, dog, pig and chicken), impacts on the introduction of foreign plants and animals, the intense agricultural development during the middle Neolithic, the population growth and forthcoming social change during the Yangshao and Longshan periods, the contextual development of various craftmanship, the beginning of writing, the rise and fall of the Bronze Age dynasties, the regionalization in the Eastern Zhou phase, changes of weapon types and ways of warfare during the Shang and Zhou era, the unification of China as an empire during the Qin and Han eras, Qin and Han secular societies from the aspects of material culture, and foreign cultures aside from the Huaxia civilized world.",
    "pre_subname": "",
    "pre_sub_id3": null,
    "pre_sub_ename": "",
    "pre_describe": null,
    "pre_describe_en": null,
    "scr_credit": 2.0
  },
  "targets": [
    {
      "seq": 1,
      "describe_ch": "了解上古時期中國文化的起源、發展脈絡與今日華人文化傳統的相關性",
      "describe_en": "To acquire basic knowledge on the connections among the origins, cultural and contextual development of ancient Chinese culture, together with the cultural tradition of present-day Chinese world."
    },
    {
      "seq": 2,
      "describe_ch": "藉由古代文物背後之文化脈絡瞭解探索文化創新",
      "describe_en": "To explore the potential capacity of cultural innovation through the understanding of cultural context behind ancient cultural relics."
    }
  ],
